  BDD/TDD test proposals (2026.05.17)
  
  1. Stage 8 — Routing Grid (planned, no code, no tests)

  The CLAUDE.md spec is detailed. These tests define the API contract before implementation:

  Feature file: routing_grid.feature
  Scenarios needed: TrackPattern pitch/density calculation; def_track_pattern CLI
  round-trip;
    signal_tracks_in(lo, hi) returns only SIGNAL slots; power/clock slots correctly block
    signal placement; PatternOverride region takes precedence over global; edge case: region

    boundary — slot straddles override boundary

  TDD unit tests in test_routing_grid.py: unit_pitch(), signal_density(), dilution_factor(),
   tracks_in_range() with known patterns (VDD/sig/sig/sig/GND/sig/sig/sig repeating unit).

  ---
  2. Stage 9 — Detailed NUTS (planned, no code, no tests)
  
  detailed_track_assignment.feature already has three placeholder scenarios but they target
  abstract concepts (VIC pull, corner margins, non-uniform width). They need to be rewritten
   to match the actual designed API:

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │              Scenario               │                What to assert                 │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ run_detailed_nuts expands           │ len(net_segments) == bit_width for each       │
  │ BusSegment → N NetSegments          │ BusSegment                                    │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ LO_HI bit ordering assigns          │ net_segments[i].track_position <              │
  │ contiguous tracks low-to-high       │ net_segments[i+1].track_position              │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ HI_LO bit ordering is the reverse   │ same, flipped                                 │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ timing_critical flag finds          │ no PreRoutedSegment between any two           │
  │ contiguous window (no power/clock   │ consecutive NetSegments in the window         │
  │ between bits)                       │                                               │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Pre-route blockage forces placement │ no NetSegment lands on a POWER or CLOCK track │
  │  above/below                        │                                               │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ num_unplaced > 0 when interval has  │ assertion on DetailedNUTSResult.num_unplaced  │
  │ no contiguous window large enough   │                                               │
  └─────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ---
  3. MST / Multi-trunk topologies (roadmap, feature stub exists)
  
  large_fanout_mst.feature has three scenarios but they're vague ("significantly less
  wirelength"). Replace with concrete assertions:

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                  Scenario                   │          Concrete assertion           │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ MST for 1-driver, 4-receiver fanout         │ total wirelength ≤ bounding-box       │
  │                                             │ diagonal × 1.5 (Steiner ratio bound)  │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ MST produces N-1 edges for N nodes          │ len(topology.segments) is bounded     │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Multi-trunk topology selected over          │ planner picks BITRUNK or MST type     │
  │ single-trunk when channel is congested      │ over L/Z when single-trunk overflow > │
  │                                             │  0                                    │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Multicast generate_topologies_for_bundle    │ topology type starts with MST_ or     │
  │ with 3 destinations                         │ BITRUNK_                              │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┘

  ---
  4. Post-NUTS planner (implemented, no dedicated tests)
  
  run_planner post_nuts V <short> <long> has no test at all — it's currently only exercised
  by ariane_core.buda. Needed:

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                 Scenario                 │                  Assert                  │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Short V stubs (< threshold) are moved to │ seg previously on M7 reassigned to M3/M5 │
  │  a lower V layer                         │  after post_nuts                         │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Long V stubs (> threshold) stay on high  │ seg on M7 remains M7                     │
  │ V layer                                  │                                          │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ H variant works symmetrically            │ same for H-layer stubs                   │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ post_nuts without prior run_nuts errors  │ raises/prints error, doesn't crash       │
  │ gracefully                               │                                          │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ---
  5. run_nuts_on_layer / rerun isolation (implemented, no isolation test)

  ┌──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │             Scenario             │                      Assert                      │
  ├──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Rerunning M5 does not disturb M4 │ all M4 track_position values unchanged           │
  │  placements                      │ before/after rerun_layer(5)                      │
  ├──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Rerun reduces overlaps on target │ num_overlaps on M5 ≤ pre-rerun count             │
  │  layer                           │                                                  │
  └──────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ---
  6. CLI integration tests (no .buda-level tests exist)
  
  All current tests call C++ directly. End-to-end tests exercising buda_cli.py catch
  integration bugs (like the two.buda case, which had no test):

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                Test                 │                    Script                     │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ two.buda produces 0 overlaps        │ run two.buda, assert nuts_result.num_overlaps │
  │                                     │  == 0                                         │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ ariane.buda runs without violation  │ assert num_violations == 0                    │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ ariane_core.buda runs with ≤ 3      │ assert known bound                            │
  │ overlaps                            │                                               │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ source command includes nested      │ inline source in temp script, assert it       │
  │ script                              │ executes                                      │
  └─────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┘

